.SH NAME
ktm-bytes \- A queue of bytes for binary data that comes and goes in pieces.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
import bytes;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
A queue of bytes for binary data that comes and goes in pieces.
.SH TYPES
.SS Buffer
.EX
struct Buffer
{
    u8 *ptr;
    i64 start;
    i64 len;
    i64 cap;
};
.EE
.PP
A growable queue of bytes: append at the end, consume from the front. For what a socket or a file gives in pieces (read into room(), parse data(), consume() what was used) and for building binary messages (appendBe32(...), then data() or take()). Make one with bytes.bufferNew() or declare one (it starts empty), free it with b.free(). Its fields are read-only outside module bytes.
